Audit Verdict
PR #211 is a well-engineered persistence layer attached to a funnel that emits no measurement at all. The backend work is among the most disciplined in the repository. The conversion-tracking surface for /wmchat is empty by deliberate design, and one of the three post-capture actions it builds is switched off in the UI.

The persistence contract — strict envelope validation, service-role-only RPC, first-write immutability, a trigger that fails closed against stale whole-document writers, and identity re-verification on both sides of the write — is correct and defensible. Nothing in this PR introduces a client-side tracking SDK, a premature conversion, or a consent regression.

The problems are not defects in what was built. They are gaps between what was built and what can be observed, reached, or optimized: a funnel invisible to every ad platform, a completed vertical hidden behind a hard-coded false, a 14-step path competing with a 3-step path, and a CI configuration under which none of the 2,000+ lines of new frontend tests actually execute.

