Recovery gap — High

Progress is saved on every state change (WmChatPage.tsx:103–105) but is only read back when the URL carries ?r= or ?resume_token=. A plain refresh, an accidental back-out, an app switch that evicts the tab, or a re-click on the same ad all restart the conversation at entry — while a complete, valid, non-PII snapshot sits unused in localStorage for 24 hours. Confirmed

Nothing in the codebase generates a ?r= link. The resume feature is, in practice, unreachable by an ordinary user. Inferred — no link generator found in repo-wide search; classified Inferred because an external system could mint such a URL.

Browser back is not intercepted; the flow is a single route with no history entries per step, so the OS/browser back gesture exits /wmchat entirely rather than stepping back one question. In-flow reversal is available only through the in-page Back control. Inferred — no history.pushState, useBlocker, or per-step navigation exists in the feature.

